bergamota: berga USB vendor interface for the host tools (WebUSB, WinUSB)

Interface 2 (class ff/62/01, bulk 0x03 OUT / 0x83 IN) next to CDC-ECM, for
tools/berga (CLI, desktop app, the website over WebUSB); protocol in
docs/BERGA_USB.md. Frames: "BRG1", 20-byte header, JSON head, raw body.

* Composite device: class EF/02/01 with an IAD around the ECM pair; bcdUSB
  2.10 with a BOS: USB 2.0 extension (no LPM), WebUSB platform capability
  (vendor request 1, landing page https://bergamota.zesmoi.com.br/manage/)
  and MS OS 2.0 (vendor request 2: WINUSB for interface 2), so Chrome/Edge
  claim it on macOS, Linux and Windows without drivers.
* The kernel answers HELLO, REBOOT (normal/fastboot/bergamota/recovery via
  kern.bergamota_reboot_mode, poweroff = RB_HALT -> 1036 PSCI SYSTEM_OFF)
  and the console log stream (LOG_START/LOG_STOP) itself. Every other request
  goes whole to /dev/berga (root, one opener) for the phone daemon (bergad);
  its response frames come back through write(). No daemon: error frame.
* One frame per transfer; a frame whose length is a multiple of 512 carries
  one pad byte (flag PAD) so every transfer ends in a short packet.
* DMA area 0x4000 -> 0x24000 (64 KiB per direction); physical endpoints 6/7
  (TX FIFO 3); FIFOs of 256 KiB each way; kern.bergamota_berga counters.
  Boot-arg bergamotaberga=0 leaves the interface without a backend.
VID/PID stay 1209:0001 (pid.codes test ID, placeholder).
